From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - Geom_BezierSurface IsURational/IsVRational
 prose contradicts its own example matrix

Geom_BezierSurface.hxx says

  //! Returns False if the weights are identical in the U direction,
  //! Example :
  //!               |1.0, 1.0, 1.0|
  //! if Weights =  |0.5, 0.5, 0.5|   returns False
  //!               |2.0, 2.0, 2.0|
  Standard_EXPORT bool IsURational() const;

The weights in that matrix are not identical in the U direction, they run
1.0, 0.5, 2.0 down a column. They are identical in the V direction. So the
prose and the example contradict each other, and the example is the one that
matches the code.

Geom_BezierSurface.cxx's static Rational() sets Urational from

  Urational = (std::abs(Weights(I, J) - Weights(I, J + 1)) > Epsilon(...));

inside a loop over I that walks J, so the comparison is between neighbours in
the column index, which is V. Urational is therefore false exactly when every
row of the weight matrix is constant, and Vrational is false exactly when every
column is. Each flag names the axis opposite the one it compares along.

Geom_BSplineSurface.hxx already states this correctly, with the same two
example matrices:

  //! Returns False if for each row of weights all the weights
  //! are identical.

so the two headers currently disagree with one another as well as one of them
disagreeing with the implementation. This change gives Geom_BezierSurface the
wording Geom_BSplineSurface already has, leaving the example matrices and the
tolerance sentence untouched.

Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with four explicit weight matrices: rows
constant gives (IsURational, IsVRational) = (0, 1), columns constant gives
(1, 0), all weights equal gives (0, 0), and varying along both gives (1, 1).
A Geom_BSplineSurface converted from a cylinder reports (0, 1) and (1, 0) after
ExchangeUV(), the same way round.

Documentation only, no behaviour change. Geom_BezierSurface.cxx was compiled
against the corrected header on all three slices to confirm it still builds.

The probe is Scripts/repro/2976-surface-rational-axes/probe.mm in the OCCTSwift
repository. OCCTSwift issue #2991.

diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_BezierSurface.hxx b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_BezierSurface.hxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_BezierSurface.hxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Geom/Geom_BezierSurface.hxx
@@ -561,7 +561,8 @@ public:
   //! Returns False.
   Standard_EXPORT bool IsVPeriodic() const final;

-  //! Returns False if the weights are identical in the U direction,
+  //! Returns False if for each row of weights all the weights
+  //! are identical.
   //! The tolerance criterion is Resolution from package gp.
   //! Example :
   //! |1.0, 1.0, 1.0|
@@ -569,7 +570,8 @@ public:
   //! |2.0, 2.0, 2.0|
   Standard_EXPORT bool IsURational() const;

-  //! Returns False if the weights are identical in the V direction,
+  //! Returns False if for each column of weights all the weights
+  //! are identical.
   //! The tolerance criterion is Resolution from package gp.
   //! Example :
   //! |1.0, 2.0, 0.5|
